REQ-POPULATION-003,IMPLEMENTED,596,597,,"PR #597 implements Handoff/06 Phase-9 household realization and economic evidence: positive-population cohorts consume the single canonical householdInventory against stable priority-ordered need categories, use candidate qualityFactor as the per-unit useful-equivalent conversion, compute bounded category coverage and canonical essentialCoverage, and share one working inventory so overlapping categories cannot double-consume physical stock. Realized Phase-8 MAIN purchases are projected only during immutable-tick planning; applyHouseholdConsumptionTransition refuses persistence unless canonical market settlement has already produced that exact post-market stock, so Phase 9 never becomes a second settlement path. Excess carryover above required useful consumption times inventoryCarryoverTicks destroys only eligible perishable stock and emits explicit HOUSEHOLD_SPOILAGE transaction plus PHYSICAL_LOSS(spoilage) evidence; consumption likewise emits attributed one-sided physical loss while durable excess is retained. Economic evidence reuses LaborSupplyPlan availability, Phase-3 LaborAllocation employment/gross obligations, Phase-5 WageSettlement and exact WAGE_PAYMENT transaction net receipts, validating gross = net + collected withholding without rematching labor or recomputing tax/transfers. Focused regressions in src/simulation/householdConsumptionExecution.test.ts prove shortage/no-negative inventory, canonical essential coverage, perishable spoilage and durable retention, overlapping-good single use, Phase-8 settlement precondition, employment/wage reconciliation and malformed wage rejection, insertion-order equivalence, TickContext-only handler behavior and input-world immutability. Phase-13 demography/migration, household resale/replanning, M5+ behavior and mirror edits remain out of scope."
